The ported files keep the Apache License 2.0 header and say what changed:

- src/role-utils.ts: packages/playwright-core/src/server/injected/roleUtils.ts
  (ivya src/roleUtils.ts). Changed: the imports; a DOM that does not render,
  of Node.js, has no content of pseudo-elements; `isElementHiddenForAria()`
  and `getAriaDisabled()` skip a walk up the tree whose answer is known;
  `getAriaRoleCandidates()`, `getPlainTextAccessibleName()` and
  `getPlainTextContent()` are added.
- src/dom-utils.ts: packages/playwright-core/src/server/injected/domUtils.ts
  (ivya src/domUtils.ts), and `sortInDOMOrder()` of selectorEvaluator.ts.
  Changed: WebKit is detected by the user agent instead of an option; in a
  DOM that does not render, of Node.js, a style without a visibility is
  visible; `hasVisibleBox()` is added.
- src/text-match.ts: `normalizeWhiteSpace()` of
  packages/playwright-core/src/utils/isomorphic/stringUtils.ts,
  `matchesAttributePart()`, `elementText()`, `elementMatchesText()` and
  `getElementLabels()` of packages/playwright-core/src/server/injected/selectorUtils.ts,
  and `createTextMatcher()` of injectedScript.ts (ivya src/ivya.ts).
  Changed: the matchers take a locator's arguments instead of a selector.
- src/selectors.ts: the role engine of roleSelectorEngine.ts; the text,
  label and attribute engines of injectedScript.ts (ivya src/ivya.ts); the
  selectors of packages/playwright-core/src/utils/isomorphic/locatorUtils.ts
  and the escapes of stringUtils.ts; the printing of locatorGenerators.ts.
  Changed: the engines take a locator's arguments instead of a selector
  string; the role engine looks at the candidates of a role only.

